# Set the goal the epistemic state holds.
#
# The counterpart of the problem expert's goal, one level up. A PDDL goal says
# what must be true; this one says what must be known — "(Kw c1 muddy_c1)",
# every child knows whether it is muddy — which no set of predicates records.
#
# It is the state's goal rather than the planner's because the state is where
# the vocabulary lives: a goal is checked against a model, and a formula naming
# an agent or atom the loaded task does not have is a mistake worth catching
# when it is set rather than when a plan is asked for.

# The goal, in the grammar the policy carries and check_formula accepts.
# Empty restores the goal of the loaded task, which is what the state starts
# with.
string goal
---
bool success
string error

# Whether the new goal already holds in the current state. A goal that is
# satisfied the moment it is set is worth knowing about: it means there is
# nothing to plan for.
bool holds
